<theodulf. carm. 77.1>	Terra marique victor honorande,
<theodulf. carm. 77.2>	Caesar auguste Hludowice, Christi
<theodulf. carm. 77.3>	Dogmate clarus, decus aevi nostri,
<theodulf. carm. 77.4>	Spes quoque regni;
<theodulf. carm. 77.5>	Quamvis adventus sit ubique tuus
<theodulf. carm. 77.6>	Laude perenni rite celebrandus,
<theodulf. carm. 77.7>	Cui totus orbis voto, fide bona
<theodulf. carm. 77.8>	Cuncta precatur,
<theodulf. carm. 77.9>	Urbs tamen ista votis antecellit
<theodulf. carm. 77.10>	Ceteras urbes Galliae comatae;
<theodulf. carm. 77.11>	Cernere longos valeas ut annos
<theodulf. carm. 77.12>	Clamat ubique.
<theodulf. carm. 77.13>	Patris Martini meritis et aucta
<theodulf. carm. 77.14>	Munere vestro, celebris in orbe,
<theodulf. carm. 77.15>	Ceteris praestat Galliae praefatae
<theodulf. carm. 77.16>	Urbs quoque nostra.
<theodulf. carm. 77.17>	Fulgeas claris per regna triumphis,
<theodulf. carm. 77.18>	Gentes sub tuis pedibus iniquas
<theodulf. carm. 77.19>	Felix consternas, quae tibi repugnant
<theodulf. carm. 77.20>	Subdere colla.
<theodulf. carm. 77.21>	Invidus hostis laedere dum temptat
<theodulf. carm. 77.22>	Foedera iuris, animos movendo,
<theodulf. carm. 77.23>	Prosperitatem semper tibi favet,
<theodulf. carm. 77.24>	Maxime princeps,
<theodulf. carm. 77.25>	Omne per ceptum iter ire quibis
<theodulf. carm. 77.26>	Ecce donante domino securus:
<theodulf. carm. 77.27>	Pro te pugnabit, rex bone, Martinus
<theodulf. carm. 77.28>	Atleta fortis.
<theodulf. carm. 77.29>	Caeli directus angelus ab arce
<theodulf. carm. 77.30>	Prosper, optamus, ducat ac reducat
<theodulf. carm. 77.31>	Terras, per silvas, per castella, vicos
<theodulf. carm. 77.32>	Semper euntem.
<theodulf. carm. 77.33>	Vale Ermengardis, regina et augusta,
<theodulf. carm. 77.34>	Et tui tecum in seculo nati:
<theodulf. carm. 77.35>	Idcirco nostri in dulcedine cordis
<theodulf. carm. 77.36>	Semper habemus.
<theodulf. carm. 77.37>	Annuis pia miseratione,
<theodulf. carm. 77.38>	Servulis tuis solatia praestans
